## Always-on demo — a tool-only "heartbeat" bot relaunched continuously by
## an `overlap: keepalive` schedule (host crontab, >=1m) or a `kind: keepalive`
## invocation (resident scheduler, sub-minute). No LLM, no API keys: each run
## is a fresh, individually-budgeted process, and the keepalive policy keeps
## exactly one alive at a time, relaunching a stale one. See
## docs/scheduling.md#always-on-agents--overlap-keepalive.

schema out:
  beat: string

tool beat:
  command: `printf '{"beat":"%s"}' "$(date -u +%H:%M:%SZ)"`
  output: out

workflow heartbeat:
  entry: beat
  beat -> done
